# Docker Container Command Execution

When executing `npm`, `composer`, or `php artisan` commands, you MUST first enter the Docker container and navigate to the project directory.

## Required Steps

Before running any of these commands:
1. Enter the container: `docker-compose exec myapp bash`
2. Navigate to the project directory: `cd /var/www/html/lang-note`
3. Then execute the actual command

## Command Format

For npm commands:
```bash
docker-compose exec myapp bash -c "cd /var/www/html/lang-note && npm <command>"
```

For composer commands:
```bash
docker-compose exec myapp bash -c "cd /var/www/html/lang-note && composer <command>"
```

For php artisan commands:
```bash
docker-compose exec myapp bash -c "cd /var/www/html/lang-note && php artisan <command>"
```

## Alternative: Interactive Shell

If you need to run multiple commands or prefer an interactive session:
1. Run: `docker-compose exec myapp bash`
2. Then: `cd /var/www/html/lang-note`
3. Execute your commands in the interactive shell

## Important Notes

- The container service name is `myapp`
- The project directory inside the container is `/var/www/html/lang-note`
- Always use the combined command format (`bash -c "cd ... && command"`) when running single commands
- Use interactive shell when you need to run multiple commands sequentially
